 },
 {
  "title": "Revisiting quantization: FP8 on new GPUs",
  "create_time": 1786561920.0,
  "update_time": 1786562100.0,
  "mapping": {
   "7a6f578c-7101-cb90-ac82-c8a2b11e4cf6": {
    "id": "7a6f578c-7101-cb90-ac82-c8a2b11e4cf6",
    "message": null,
    "parent": null,
    "children": [
     "b1d46535-83f4-4f32-7ec4-40092e391df2"
    ]
   },
   "b1d46535-83f4-4f32-7ec4-40092e391df2": {
    "id": "b1d46535-83f4-4f32-7ec4-40092e391df2",
    "message": {
     "id": "b1d46535-83f4-4f32-7ec4-40092e391df2",
     "author": {
      "role": "user"
     },
     "create_time": 1786561920.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "Is FP8 inference worth it compared to int8 or AWQ 4-bit?"
      ]
     }
    },
    "parent": "7a6f578c-7101-cb90-ac82-c8a2b11e4cf6",
    "children": [
     "13037ff8-ad2a-c19a-d554-be631fb06537"
    ]
   },
   "13037ff8-ad2a-c19a-d554-be631fb06537": {
    "id": "13037ff8-ad2a-c19a-d554-be631fb06537",
    "message": {
     "id": "13037ff8-ad2a-c19a-d554-be631fb06537",
     "author": {
      "role": "assistant"
     },
     "create_time": 1786562100.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "On GPUs with FP8 Tensor Cores (Hopper, Ada, Blackwell), FP8 weights and activations give close to fp16 quality with about twice the throughput, and vLLM supports FP8 checkpoints and FP8 KV cache. AWQ 4-bit still wins on memory, so on a 12 GB consumer GPU it remains the practical option for 7B models. The choice is memory-bound versus compute-bound: quantization accelerates decoding mostly by reducing memory traffic."
      ]
     }
    },
    "parent": "b1d46535-83f4-4f32-7ec4-40092e391df2",
    "children": []
   }
  },
  "current_node": "13037ff8-ad2a-c19a-d554-be631fb06537",
  "conversation_id": "4fa9a890-d6de-1b05-0492-459c6478c498"
 }
